  "_expected_fail": {
    "exitRejectsZeroReceiver": {
      "reason": "finding",
      "detail": "withdraw/redeem with receiver == address(0) succeed. SavingsDai._burn never checks the receiver; it calls DaiJoin.exit(address(0), assets), which calls Dai.mint(address(0), assets), and mainnet DAI's mint accepts address(0). The DAI is credited to address(0), so nobody can spend it (it is effectively burned) while the owner's shares are burned. Nothing on this path depends on chi, so the zero-receiver path is reachable for any chi value. The prover CEXs are the zero-amount calls withdraw(0, 0, owner) / redeem(0, 0, owner). For illustration only, the satisfy witness exitToZeroReceiverWitness (VERIFIED) shows a positive amount, from a state where the structural invariants hold and chi >= RAY (its chi is ~5.9e76, not a realistic value): caller 0x2380 with allowance spends 1 share of owner 0x8200 in withdraw(12, address(0), 0x8200), and Dai.balanceOf(0) goes 7 -> 19. Impact: a user-error footgun that loses the withdrawn DAI. It is asymmetric with deposit/mint, which reject receiver 0 and SavingsDai (invalidReceiverRejected). ERC-4626 does not mandate the check, so this is a low-severity robustness/UX finding, not a theft vector: only the owner or an approved spender can trigger it, and only to their own loss. Out of this property's scope: receiver == SavingsDai is a second unrecoverable sink (DAI minted to sDAI cannot be moved out by any sDAI function)."
    }
  },
  "_justification_rules": {
    "potChiNeverDecreases": "supports the requirePotChiAtLeastRay trust assumption used in withdrawAccounting and mintWithdrawRoundtripNoProfit",
    "daiSupplyIsSumPreserved": "pass 2: proves every state-changing Dai entry point (transfer, transferFrom, mint, burn, approve, push, pull, move, rely, deny, permit) preserves Dai.totalSupply == ghost sum of Dai balances. No vault rule consumes requireDaiSupplyIsSum anymore (the real Dai's checked add makes a wrap revert, not succeed), so it is retained as a proven fact about the DAI model, not as a justification for any bare require.",
    "exitToZeroReceiverWitness": "pass 3: a satisfy rule (VERIFIED = scenario reachable) that witnesses the exitRejectsZeroReceiver finding with a positive amount: withdraw(assets > 0, receiver = address(0)) succeeds, burns > 0 shares from owner and credits Dai.balanceOf(0) with exactly assets. It is not a property rule; VERIFIED here confirms the finding.",
    "convertToAssetsBoundReachable": "pass 4 (probe conf erc4626-rpow-probe.conf): satisfy rule (VERIFIED = reachable) showing convertToAssets runs to completion at the largest covered exponent t - rho = 2^loop_iter - 1 = 15 with dsr > RAY, i.e. the optimistic loop unrolling does not prune the covered range.",
    "rpowBoundReachable": "pass 4 (probe conf): same coverage witness for the verbatim RpowHarness.rpow at n = 15.",
